.nh
.TH "PB-STATUS" "1" "Sep 2026" "Paperboat" "Paperboat CLI"

.SH NAME
pb-status - Show local Paperboat machine status


.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBpb status [machine] [flags]\fP


.SH DESCRIPTION
Show this machine's Paperboat state, or the observed status of the machine you name. It is
a snapshot, not a wait: use pb doctor for a deeper check, pb service status for the background
service and pb wait to wait for a condition. On a machine that is waiting to be added, status
reports the signed-out state; run pb login.

.PP
JSON output is supported with --json.


.SH OPTIONS
\fB-h\fP, \fB--help\fP[=false]
	help for status

.PP
\fB--json\fP[=false]
	print JSON


.SH OPTIONS INHERITED FROM PARENT COMMANDS
\fB--config\fP=""
	path to the CLI config file

.PP
\fB--no-customization\fP[=false]
	ignore local shortcuts, command defaults, and TUI preferences

.PP
\fB--server\fP=""
	paperboat-server base URL override

.PP
\fB--workspace\fP=""
	resource workspace selector: personal or a team slug


.SH EXAMPLE
.EX
  pb status
  pb status studio
  pb status --json
.EE


.SH SEE ALSO
\fBpb(1)\fP
